thinking about your next vacation what  if I told you there's no need to wait  for next year thanks to the retro land  theme park an animal crossing new  horizons five-star amusement park start  your day at the teacup ride while  parents sip on their morning coffee next  catch the superstars of wrestling as  they Duke it out in the smash arena then  grab a snack or beverage at one of our  many dining options located in the  center of food court and enjoy live  music as you do spend your afternoon  relaxing by the pool don't forget the  kids playground which features a rock  climbing wall sandbox and more then cap  off your day with some fun and games at  the retro land arcade now get ready I'm  about to give you a full breakdown of  how the park was created demolished and  then rebuilt again from scratch people  of the Internet retro records who are  here your guide to family-friendly  content in the world of video games so a  couple of weeks ago I published this  video and to be honest I was pretty  proud of the theme park we'd created  what if I told you I'd completely  demolished nearly all of the old theme  park and built a new one from scratch  well that's exactly what I did and now I  just have to share the new and improved  version with you if you stick around to  the end you'll see just how it has  completely changed in so many different  ways guys it's it's crazy now this just  so happens to be my favorite spot on my  island but I'm curious to hear from you  guys what creations are you most proud  of so far or what are you hoping to  create let me know down in the comments  I'd love to hear what you all are  creating and by the way guys our island  is now officially a five-star island  obviously others hit this milestone much  faster but my son and I have really been  playing at our own pace and not getting  into too big a rush and I could not be  prouder of where we're at well as from a  new theme park this is the focal point  of our five-star island and it all  starts with the entrance you can see one  of our first upgrades right from the  start with the new metal red ramp which  replaces the old blue wooden one we had  previously also much more organization  to the flowers this go-round  what's funny is I joked last time about  us having two mini flowers but I  actually used nearly all of them up here  in the revamp they're just way more  spread out as you'll see throughout the  video you've probably already noticed we  switched to the Imperial fence as well  which I think matches the ramp into the  park quite nicely  as you enter you'll see the two  marketplace flags on both sides and also  a stone arch as you make your way  forward two booths on either side as  well with one booth having magic hat and  the bingo roller drum thingy yeah I  included two fountains on either side of  the entrance as I think these fountains  look really good in a variety of  locations I have several of them on my  island and they're definitely one of the  most versatile items you can use now as  you make your way to the central area of  the amusement park you'll quickly  realize the entire area has now been  based around this central hub which  serves as a food court I also put the  teacup ride right smack in the middle as  I feel it's such an important item to  the overall space a lot of the items in  here I'm kind of stretching to make work  with a theme park setting but the teacup  ride really sets the tone nicely and it  also has the musical element which I  think is perfect in the previous video I  mentioned that the food court was my  favorite area so I've moved it front and  center here and have also provided more  seating this time all of our food  options are still here pizza popcorn  cotton candy and more restrooms and  trash cans are still important as always  however we found a nice little spot over  here to the side to tuck them out of the  way  after all you need convenience of them  nearby your food area but you really 